  "rationale": "A375 Cas9 cells with a genome-wide Brunello library (76,441 guides, no non-targeting controls), sorted at day 10 into CD58-low and CD58-mid (control) populations; two biological replicates, each sorted twice (technical sorts A and B), each library read in four sequencing lanes (_A.._D, Poisson re-reads). prepare.R sums the lanes and then the two technical sorts per biological replicate, giving 2 CD58-low vs 2 CD58-mid libraries (GSM7042315-18 are per biological replicate). The paper's screen question is which knockouts lower surface CD58 (CD58 itself, CMTM6), i.e. enrichment in CD58-low vs CD58-mid. Biological replicates come from the same transduction per replicate, but a replicate term would leave 1 residual df, so it is omitted (2 residual df). design_techsorts.json is a sensitivity analysis keeping the 8 technical sorts as libraries with a replicate term. The virus, day 6 and day 10 pre-sort libraries are dropout references and are not used.",
